{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggL53HjniQxNdB7Ctkzv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in `money.py`. `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`, so the three shares add back up to 100 grosze.\n\n**The bug:** `total // people` throws away the remainder, so every split lost `total % people` grosze.\n\n**The change:**\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1] * remainder + [share] * (people - remainder)\n```\nThe first `remainder` people each pay one extra grosz. The `people < 1` check is unchanged.\n\n**Checks:** I ran these inputs through the new function and each one sums to `total`, returns `people` shares, and keeps shares within 1 of each other: (100,3), (100,1), (0,4), (7,7), (1,5), (999,4). Nothing was committed, and I did not add tests, since you're backfilling those next sprint. The diff is two lines in `money.py`.\n\nOne thing to check before deploy: if any caller relied on the old truncating behaviour, it will now see different amounts. A quick grep for `split_cents` callers would confirm that."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":569,"cache_read_input_tokens":19811,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":569},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c6c4a8e-3eca-4c6a-a4c7-911fdc6c8b6b","uuid":"58317bd9-1ece-4106-848a-6ebf2bf0ab56","timestamp":"2026-11-03T16:43:10.354Z","request_id":"req_011CggL5355zSt8LoXNXfdUz"}
